                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4be2fca4-af59-3195-8b52-b9e837e4900a",
                        "entry_id": "548510ca-eef3-350e-ae43-68c4783a3db0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To cover or line the underside of (a floor or roof) with plasterwork, boarding or other such treatment."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "94ad07ac-2fd7-47f5-ad09-40ec0d2b895d",
                                "sense_id": "4be2fca4-af59-3195-8b52-b9e837e4900a",
                                "text": "The [roof] had never been underdrawn, its entire anatomy lay bare to an inquiring eye, except where a frame of wood laden with oatcakes, and clusters of legs of beef, mutton and ham, concealed it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46c91a2e-bfb9-4f7a-9664-23b09f7c9e6b",
                                "sense_id": "4be2fca4-af59-3195-8b52-b9e837e4900a",
                                "text": "He has the whole of the room underdrawn, with the exception of two bays at one end; he admits plenty of air by the windows in the roof into the triangular shaped space formed by the roof and the underdrawing;"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "01a0ead5-4381-37fc-a851-8adec48f32ca",
                        "entry_id": "548510ca-eef3-350e-ae43-68c4783a3db0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To take or draw less than one needs or is entitled to."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3829e18-0eea-426f-a63e-16604c76f8f1",
                                "sense_id": "01a0ead5-4381-37fc-a851-8adec48f32ca",
                                "text": "You say for month and months you had been underdrawing? — Always underdrawing and giving up every month. Whatever we drew the officer signed an indent for and we gave up a surplus."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "02c16f5e-e678-31b0-be49-f81388779c6c",
                        "entry_id": "548510ca-eef3-350e-ae43-68c4783a3db0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To represent inadequately in an artistic depiction, or in words."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "59168c03-5f42-3df3-8bde-0f9869c6966c",
                        "entry_id": "548510ca-eef3-350e-ae43-68c4783a3db0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To sketch a work of art in chalk, pencil, or other temporary medium prior to painting, inking, or otherwise making the final work."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "edd422be-1a3a-49c6-b136-1e5d6e181d72",
                                "sense_id": "59168c03-5f42-3df3-8bde-0f9869c6966c",
                                "text": "Here was the warrant (or at least a justification) not just for Steig's drawings of people as bodily symptoms but, more important, for his abandoning underdrawing in pencil prepartory to inking in a drawing."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
